            <ArticleTitle>Left bundle branch block and right axis deviation due to severe coronary heart disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>413-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The simultaneous occurrence of left bundle branch block and right axis deviation is very rare and occurs mainly in patients with cardiomyopathy. This paper describes a 61-year-old man with end stage ischaemic heart disease who presented with this unique electrocardiographic abnormality.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
